{"t":8787,"type":"chat","data":{"kind":"html","chatId":"d8c152da-0679-454e-be31-06c4af46f2c4","messageId":245,"html":"<h2>Goal</h2><ul><li>Understand what a KV cache is.</li><li>Fetch content from a specific URL and report a specific field.</li></ul><h2>Established</h2><ul><li>KV cache = memory structure in transformer-based language models storing computed key and value vectors for each token processed so far.</li><li>Benefits: avoids recomputation during autoregressive token generation, trades memory for speed.</li><li>Fetched https://httpbin.org/delay/4 (4-second delay endpoint).</li><li>The <code>url</code> field in the JSON response = &quot;https://</li></ul>","htmlAt":474}}
